{"kind":"request","text":"Document and enforce the Gitseq kernel-application boundary\n\nCreate docs/reference/architecture.md as the canonical account of Gitseq's layers. Distinguish the semantic-free kernel from replaceable application profiles, and identify Workroom - including its fold, projections, tools, guidance, connectors, and UI - as the first application rather than Gitseq's ontology. Update SKILL.md so exact-head implementation review explicitly checks this contract.","body":{"branch":"request/architecture-layering","conditions":"1. Add docs/reference/architecture.md with normal front matter and list it in docs/README.md; rest it on the current implementation artifacts.\n2. Define ordinary Git storage, kernel, nexus/live runtime, application profile/interpreter, projections/queries, and CLI/MCP/skill/connectors/UI surfaces.\n3. Kernel owns genesis/sequence, actor-key attribution and signatures, sequencer admission/signatures, opaque schema/payload binding, signed rests_on, ordering, idempotency, bounds, verification, and key rotation.\n4. Kernel does not understand names/membership/kinds/roles; commitments or ratification/supersession semantics; artifacts/reviews/staleness/work status; or UI workflows.\n5. Workroom is the current application: governed vocabulary and schemas, fold, authority, commitments/artifacts, guarded commands, MCP, SKILL.md discipline, connectors, and UI.\n6. Separate kernel-protocol, application-family, interpreter/fold, projection-contract, and surface/UI compatibility. A missing interpreter is kernel-verifiable but application-uninterpretable; invent no fallback meaning.\n7. Map current packages and surfaces to layers, stating current coupling and intended boundaries.\n8. Use artifact terms precisely: the kernel has no artifact ontology; Workroom projects path@commit, retirement, and staleness.\n9. Add a concise mandatory SKILL.md rule: every implementation review names affected architecture layers; the reviewer says whether the exact head preserves or changes the contract. A changed contract must update and re-anchor the page in that same head; otherwise request changes, not approval.\n10. Verify make docs, make test, and git diff --check. Record the page's first exact-head artifact on the current implementation bases; it has no predecessor.","to":"5f12e916d136b0c1ed941aa99f4c47af94021451e31d08159d8df368e9946123"}}